was such a meaningless clip, David, because

00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:31.970
it's a hypothetical.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:33.280
That's just that guy's opinion.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.340
There is no such situation.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.270
And his opinion isn't the law in Mississippi
anyway, so it doesn't matter.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:42.780
Well, these are relevant hypotheticals because
they do happen.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.350
And here is a non hypothetical.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:45.350
A non.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.440
This is a real story.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.280
The Hill reports ten year old girl denied
abortion in Ohio.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.650
A ten year old girl was denied an abortion
in Ohio after the Supreme Court ruled last

00:00:55.650 --> 00:01:01.150
week that it was overturning Roe v Wade, demonstrating
the tangible impacts that the high court's

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:05.689
decision is having on patients seeking access
to the medical procedure.

00:01:05.689 --> 00:01:07.340
A child.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:09.060
This is a horrible, horrible story.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:14.409
A child abuse doctor in Ohio contacted Dr.
Caitlin Bernhardt Barnard, an obstetrician

00:01:14.409 --> 00:01:19.770
gynecologist in Indiana, after receiving a
ten year old patient.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.420
Six weeks and three days pregnant.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.670
The patient is now heading west to Indiana.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:29.350
Given that an abortion ban in Ohio, which
prohibits the medical procedure when fetal

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:35.280
cardiac activity begins around six weeks,
had become effective quickly after the high

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.319
court issued its decision.

00:01:37.319 --> 00:01:42.299
Several groups filed a lawsuit seeking to
block the state law from taking effect.

00:01:42.299 --> 00:01:47.240
On Wednesday, an emergency stay of the abortion
ban was rejected by the Ohio Supreme Court

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:51.310
Friday, meaning the ban can be upheld as the
case is reviewed.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:55.889
Ohio is among a number of states that have
rolled back abortion access since the Supreme

00:01:55.889 --> 00:01:58.549
Court eliminated the constitutional right
to an abortion.

00:01:58.549 --> 00:02:03.600
Some laws have been paused pending legal challenges,
but Indiana could soon find itself passing

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:08.009
its own abortion law later this month, given
that a special session has been scheduled

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:09.700
for later in July.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:12.180
So understand what is going on here.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:19.650
We have had all sorts of different laws around
the country over the last 50 years, quite

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:21.959
frankly, the Roe v Wade era and in fact, longer.

